Program          : DRVEC 0.12
Input Data File  : the .pre files
Output File      : e1fit.out
Model            : VARMA-VECM(2,1), M = 3 series, cointegration rank r = 1
Estimation       : Exact Unconditional Maximum Likelihood, Algorithm AS 311 (Mauricio 1997), xi sequence truncated at 1e-3
Transformation   : VECM to stationary VARMA (Mauricio 2006)
Deterministic    : case 2 -- E[nabla Y2] = 0, E[W] free
Structure        : F free, Theta free (the default; -mafree), Sigma free
Series           : invest income cons   (2 in the nabla Y2 block, 1 in Y1)
Sample           : 91 observations from 1960/2, quarterly (raw 92)

=== The ladder below the rank: r = 0, from the gate up ===
  rung 0  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma diag)   logL = 703.5254690090

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     148.1558611078
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     274.1300031938
  univariate 3 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     281.2352204638
                                 sum  =     703.5210847654
                                 joint=     703.5210806454
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is 703.5254690090)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -4.120e-06   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   *** NOT VERIFIED ***

  The two sides must agree at this rung to rounding: both are
  evaluated with the whole xi sequence.  A gap is then not
  truncation, and the fault is upstream of the likelihood --
  the transformation, the rank's differencing, the parameter
  walk, the deterministic terms or the scaling -- and never in
  elf() itself.
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = 722.3705693303
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = 768.1831505637

